{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Noah","id":"360967589511561218","is_bot":0,"username":"king.crusader"},"author_id":"360967589511561218","channel_id":"863933045849849897","content":"***A QUICK GUIDE TO RESTORATIVE JUSTICE:***\n```\nDefinition: a system of criminal justice which focuses on the rehabilitation of offenders through reconciliation with victims and the community at large. \n\n• Seeks to repair the harm done\n• Emphasizes accountability, making amends, and if agreed upon, facilitated meeting between offenders and victims.\n• Seeks to empower victims and meet their needs\n• The goal is to heal, and prevent repeat offenders from being cycled through the system\n• Often applies indigenous practices of council and justice when dealing out consequences\n• If needed, a prison would be used for reintegration into society by giving them tools to succeed\n• Community restoration and involvement is key to success \n\nExamples:\n• Community service \n• Restitution \n• Victim-offender reconciliation```","created_at":"2021-08-14T02:40:08.101000Z","edited_at":"2021-08-14T02:40:35.076000Z","id":"875931770451791943","reply_to_id":null,"thread":{"archived":1,"channel_id":"863933045849849897","created_at":"2021-08-14T01:36:34.037000Z","id":"875915773107925062","name":"Constitution Resources"},"thread_id":"875915773107925062"}
